# expect: is declared to return `number` but its body gives no value
# A function that promises an answer and gives none used to fabricate a 0.
#
# Zero is a legal id, a legal position and a legal health, so the mistake was
# never found where it was made - it was found later, somewhere else, as a
# thing that was at the origin or had no hit points. In a language sold on
# having no null, a silent zero IS a null wearing a number's clothes.
#
# The sibling case - the body answers the WRONG type - was already caught
# (wrong_return.or). This is the one where it answers nothing: a void call, a
# loop, or an `if` with no else as the last thing in the body.
define f() -> number:
    print_line("this is not an answer")

define main() -> number:
    f()
